## THE COMMISSION (RELAYED: read the two gate STATUS files WHOLE first, both in `1_Project_Definition/Briefs/`: `2026-10-23_B491_STATUS.md` (Findings, FOR TUESDAY, Check A5) and `2026-10-22_B476_STATUS.md` (Findings, Check 3 (v), 5, 10); if absent, say so, do not hunt)
Seven test gaps, every one measured by a gate as a **mutant that survives**, five of them surviving identically on the unmodified base file (so they are old oracle gaps, not weakened by #188 or #185). Two files. Where a gate's fix-shape is named, it is the gate's PROPOSAL, not a ruling.

### Group J: `api/tests/HpsmPoc.Api.Tests/Assessment/JwtBearerRolePathTests.cs` (at `fd54671a`)
- **B491-1 (Minor).** `ADDED-18` (`:75-:76`): `["ADDED-18 signed Admin, expired"] = (() => JwtBearerHostFactory.Sign(Who("expired", new[] { "Admin" }), expires: DateTime.UtcNow.AddHours(-1)), [], "401", null),`. The assertions are `:114` `Assert.True(expect == got, ...)` and `:115` `if (expect == "401") Assert.Contains(reply.Headers.WwwAuthenticate, h => h.Scheme == "Bearer");`: status 401 and a `Bearer` challenge, nothing about WHY. **Mutant MA6a** (`AddHours(-1)` -> `AddHours(1)`, anchor count 1) survives at base and at head: `Sign` sets `NotBefore = expires - 31 min` (`Support/JwtBearerHostFactory.cs:60-:62`), so a token expiring in an hour starts in 29 minutes, the host answers 401 "The token is not valid before ...", and the row reads green for the wrong reason (RELAYED, MEASURED by the gate: `expires` = now + 40 or + 60 min -> 401 "not valid before"; now + 35 or + 31.5 min -> 200). The row is NOT weakened (gate mutant MA6b, `AddMinutes(-4)`, turns it red). **Fix-shape (gate):** for the expired row assert that the challenge's reason names expiry (the `Bearer` challenge's `error_description` reads `The token expired at '...'`); ideally each 401 row its own reason. **Regression: MA6a must turn ADDED-18 red.**
- **B491-1 extension (this brief's call, bounded).** The gate measured, under the old shape and a delay, that the lifetime check runs BEFORE the audience and issuer checks: an expired token answers "The token expired" even when its audience or issuer is wrong (RELAYED, B491 table: `ADDED-16` "The audience '(null)' is invalid" at head, "The token expired" when old; `ADDED-17` "The issuer 'https://issuer.other.invalid/v2.0' is invalid" at head). So `ADDED-16` (`:71-:72`) and `ADDED-17` (`:73-:74`) can be shadowed by expiry and stay green. Pin their reasons too (the audience row names `audience`, the issuer row names `issuer`). **Not `B68-04`, `B68-05`, `B68-06`, `ADDED-19`:** the signature is validated before the lifetime, so they answer "The signature is invalid" even when expired and no clause can shadow them (RELAYED: B491 A3 table and B491-4); say in DESIGN that you left them out and why. `ADDED-14` and `ADDED-15` carry no token, so their challenge has no `error_description`: leave them.
- **B491-2 (Minor).** `:85` `public static TheoryData<string> Names() => [.. Rows.Keys];` and `:87-:92` the fact `The_matrix_holds_all_13_of_B68s_rows`, whose assertions are `:90` `Assert.Equal(13, Rows.Keys.Count(k => k.StartsWith("B68-", StringComparison.Ordinal)));` and `:91` `Assert.Equal(20, Rows.Count);`. The fact counts `Rows`, not `Names()`, so a truncated `Names()` silently runs fewer cases. **Mutant MA8** (`Names()` omits `ADDED-20`): 20 cases run, all green, the fact green (RELAYED, identical at base). **Fix-shape (gate):** make the fact assert that the theory's data source `Names()` yields exactly `Rows.Keys`, count and set. **Regression: MA8 must turn the fact red.** Choose between strengthening the existing fact in place (keeps all 21 test names byte-equal: preferred) or adding a new fact (adds one name: say so); either way no existing assertion is edited or weakened.
- **B491-3 (Note, OPTIONAL: include only if cheap; say so either way).** A committed structural test: no static field of `JwtBearerRolePathTests` holds a JWT-shaped string. The gate did this by reflection in a scratch probe (`B491PropertyProbe`: every declared static field, walk strings, tuples (`ITuple`), dictionaries and enumerables, **never invoke a delegate**, flag a string matching a three-segment base64url shape whose first segment starts `ey` + `J`; an alg-none token ends in a dot, so the third segment may be empty). RELAYED result: old file 19 holders, new file 0; controls: a planted `static readonly string` token 1, a planted dictionary of tuples holding a token 1, a planted dictionary holding `Func` recipes 0. **"Cheap" means: at most about 30 added lines, `System.Reflection` the only new `using`, no new tracked file, no flaky or slow step (it reads statics once; no clock).** If it costs more, drop it, say so in STATUS under DESIGN, and list it under Deferred. **Build the pattern at run time (parts joined), never as a literal JWT-shaped or `eyJ...` string: a literal trips gitleaks' jwt rule** (the existing `UatOpenTests.cs:386` row does the same, with a comment). Mutant **MA1** (B68-10's recipe moved back to a `static readonly string` signed at class init; the gate's own) must turn it red with NO delay and no instrument.

### Group U: `api/tests/HpsmPoc.Api.Tests/Auth/UatOpenTests.cs` (at main `42a1d92f`)
Class `UatOpenAssertionTests(UatOpenOnFactory factory) : IClassFixture<UatOpenOnFactory>` (`:311`); `RefusedRows : TheoryData<string, string?, int?>` (`:358-:363`, `Add(string why, string assertion)` and `Add(string why, int issuedOffsetSeconds)`); `public static TheoryData<string, string?, int?> Refused()` (`:365`); the rows `:373-:388`; the theory `:392-:401`: `An_assertion_that_is_not_valid_is_401(string why, string? assertion, int? issuedOffsetSeconds)` with `:397-:399` `var sent = issuedOffsetSeconds is { } offset ? UatOpenFactory.Mint("consultant", issuedAt: DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.AddSeconds(offset)) /* B472: ... */ : assertion ?? throw ...;` and `:400` `Assert.Equal(HttpStatusCode.Unauthorized, (await MeWith(sent)).Status);`. The product's window test is ONE statement, `api/src/HpsmPoc.Api/Auth/UatOpenAuthentication.cs:157`: `if (exp <= iat || exp - iat > MaxLifetimeSeconds || iat > t + SkewSeconds || exp < t - SkewSeconds) return null;` (`MaxLifetimeSeconds = 60` `:56`, `SkewSeconds = 30` `:59`).
- **B491-5 (Note, census follow-up).** `:379` `{ "lifetime over 120 s", UatOpenFactory.Mint("consultant", lifetime: 121) },` and `:380` `{ "zero lifetime", UatOpenFactory.Mint("consultant", lifetime: 0) },` are minted at DISCOVERY. Their labelled clause shares the one `if` with `exp < t - SkewSeconds`: after the discovery-minted token ages past its life plus the skew (the 121 s row after about 151 s, the zero-lifetime row after about 30 s) the row is ALSO refused by expiry, so a mutant that deletes ONLY the labelled clause survives after that horizon (RELAYED, B491 A4 (d) item 2 and B491-5; B476 Check 3 (iii) measured each row refused by its own clause alone at run time). Outcome (401) stays right; the teeth decay. **Fix-shape (gate): mint these two at run time in the body, as B472 did for `expired` and `issued beyond the skew in the future`.** Note the existing row label `lifetime over 120 s` against `MaxLifetimeSeconds = 60` is B476-5 (wording): NOT this round, leave the label byte-equal. **Regression: a scratch product mutant deleting only the lifetime clause (`exp - iat > MaxLifetimeSeconds ||`) goes RED on `lifetime over 120 s` under a discovery-to-case delay of at least the horizon; the OLD shape stays green under the same delay (survives); likewise `exp <= iat ||` for `zero lifetime`.** (A theory row cannot carry a delegate: xunit v2 cannot serialise it and would collapse the theory into one case. Carry data, as `RefusedRows` does: extend the row data by a lifetime in seconds, or any equivalent. The display name of every row changes when the signature changes, as it did at B472 (B476-4): that is accepted; the KEY is `why`, and the case count stays 16 (control: the count of enumerated cases).)
- **B476-1 (Minor).** Mutant **T2** (gate's own): `AddSeconds(offset)` -> `AddSeconds(-offset)` at `:398`: **16 of 16 green, a survivor.** A +180 s token is refused by the future clause and a -600 s token by the expiry clause, and the status-only assert cannot tell which clause refused (RELAYED: B476 Check 10 (ii)). **Fix-shape (gate, second option, the one that fits this partition):** assert, beside the 401, the sign and size of the minted token's `iat` against the clock read, from the minted token itself. The first option, "a FixedClock row per time clause in `UatOpenAssertionEdgeTests`", is NOT yours (see B476-2 and the departure below). **Regression: T2 must turn `expired` and `issued beyond the skew in the future` red.** Suggested exact form (yours to improve): read `before = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow` and `after = ...` around the mint, parse the `iat` field (the third dot-separated field, `D10`) out of `sent`, and assert `before.AddSeconds(offset).ToUnixTimeSeconds() <= iat <= after.AddSeconds(offset).ToUnixTimeSeconds()` (the mint floors with `ToUnixTimeSeconds`, so this is exact, with no tolerance and no sleep). That asserts the sign, the size and the run-time mint at once.
- **B476-2 (Minor).** No future-side skew BOUNDARY pin: `iat > t + SkewSeconds` (`:157`) is pinned by nothing tighter than the 600 s row, so the future-side skew can grow to 599 and every UatOpen test stays green (gate mutant M3c, skew 590: the future row stays green at head and base; the expiry side is pinned at 31 by `UatOpenAssertionEdgeTests.The_expiry_window_on_a_fixed_clock(-31)`, RELAYED). **Fix-shape (gate):** the fixed-clock future pair: an assertion issued `SkewSeconds` (30 s) ahead is accepted, one issued 31 s ahead is refused, on a fixed clock, with each token's life inside the maximum so that ONLY the future clause can refuse it. **The gate put it in `UatOpenAssertionEdgeTests.cs`; that file is not yours (it is outside this partition): put the pair in `UatOpenTests.cs`**, as a new `[Theory]` (or `[Fact]`s) in a class in that file that calls the public `UatOpenAuthentication.Verify(string? assertion, byte[] key, DateTimeOffset now)` (`:136`, public static) with `UatOpenFactory.Key` and a fixed instant of your own (a `DateTimeOffset` constant; no clock read, no sleep, no factory needed; or the host through `UatOpenFixedClockFactory` if you prefer the pipeline, which means you only READ `UatOpenAssertionEdgeTests.cs` and reference its public `T0`: you edit nothing there). Both must keep the label visible in the test's data (for example `[InlineData(30, "consultant")]`, `[InlineData(31, null)]`) and name the clause. **Regression: product mutants F-a, F-b, F-c, F-d below must each turn a new row red.**

**Not this round (say so in STATUS; do not build):** B476-3 (the assert argument changed `assertion` -> `sent`, accepted), B476-4 (display names), **B476-5 and B476-6 (wording)**, B491-4 (a sentence in a builder STATUS), B491-6 (the nonce in `UatOpenAssertionTests` display names: only a mask), B491-7, B491-8 to B491-13 (subject B, #184, the braces comment pair), and the MA3 / MA7 survivors (Notes: their structural check is item B491-3). No change to `api/src`, `Support/JwtBearerHostFactory.cs`, `UatOpenAssertionEdgeTests.cs`, fixtures, goldens, `web/`, `infra/`, `.github/`; no shared "mint at run time" helper; the `ClockSkew` or `SkewSeconds` values; the `Sign` default `AddMinutes(30)` at `JwtBearerHostFactory.cs:54`.

## THE FIX, stated as properties (you pick the shapes)
**Property P1 (the JWT matrix cannot pass for the wrong reason or run short):** after the change, (a) `ADDED-18` cannot read green for a token that is merely not yet valid (MA6a is red), and `ADDED-16` and `ADDED-17` cannot read green when an EARLIER validation clause (the lifetime) refuses the token (mutants MR16 and MR17 below are red); (b) `Names()` yields exactly `Rows.Keys` (a truncated, extended or duplicated `Names()` is red, MA8, MA8b, MA8c); (c) if B491-3 is taken, a static field of the class holding a JWT-shaped string is red (MA1).
**Property P2 (the UatOpen refusals keep their teeth at any run length, and the time clauses are pinned on both sides):** after the change, (a) the two lifetime rows are minted when the case runs, so each is refused ONLY by its labelled clause at any discovery-to-case delay (clause-deletion mutants L1 and L0 are red under the delay, green-surviving at the old shape); (b) the sign and size of the two time rows' offsets are pinned (T2 red; T1, T3, T4 stay red); (c) the future side of the window is pinned at the boundary (30 s accepted, 31 s refused, F-a to F-d red).
**Every new or changed assertion must be proven by a mutant that is RED with it and GREEN (surviving) without it** (measure the "without it": run each mutant against the unchanged base files first; a mutant that is red there is not a gap, say so in Corrections and drop the row). **Any change to an existing assertion is a STRENGTHENING only: print before/after for every one; never weaken, never delete, never relax a comparison; no `[Fact(Skip=...)]`, no sleep, no clock read added to a committed test beyond what P2 needs.** The 21 JwtBearer rows and the 16 `Refused()` cases keep their keys (names lost 0; for the theory the key is method plus the `why` argument).

